# Keep `tauri dev` from restarting the app on documentation edits.
#
# This crate is a path dependency of the desktop app, so the Tauri dev watcher
# watches the whole directory — including `docs/`. Saving the Quack notebook
# therefore rebuilt and restarted the app, which also rotates the generated
# Quack token and drops any client attached to it. None of these files are
# build inputs.
#
# Patterns are intentionally written without a leading slash so they match at
# any depth: the watcher roots its matcher at the common ancestor of all
# watched folders, not necessarily at this directory.
#
# NOTE: the Tauri CLI builds its ignore matcher ONCE, when `tauri dev` starts.
# Editing this file has no effect on a session that is already running — you
# have to restart `tauri dev`.

*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
docs/
*.md
